# The model a fresh install serves — the ONE place to change it.
#
# Every tracked default in the repo is asserted equal to this value by
# tests/test_default_model_pin.py, so swapping the shipped default is a one-line
# edit here plus whatever that test tells you to update.
#
# Why Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct: its hermes tool parser is already in
# deploy/model-flags.conf, and its 32768-token context clears the ~29k tokens
# Ava's own system prompt and tool schemas occupy.
#
# It does NOT fit a 16 GB card, and this comment used to say it did. The
# arithmetic: 14.2 GiB of BF16 weights against 0.90 x 16376 MiB = 14.4 GiB usable,
# so the weights fit with 0.2 GiB spare and the 32k KV cache (~2 GiB) does not.
# deploy/install.sh now needs 18000 MiB for this model and downshifts a 12-18 GB
# card to Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct rather than green-lighting an OOM.
#
# It is deliberately NOT the best model you can run — the default's job is to
# prove the install works on ordinary hardware. See docs/CHOOSE_A_MODEL.md for
# the upgrade path (Nemotron Nano 9B v2 FP8 on a 24 GB card, and up from there).
AVA_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
